 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Wudu, ghusl, tayammum: no body, no water drawn; light only on «ليطهركم». A seal for «وميثاقه», geometric for «عليم بذات الصدور». 6:22-39 (illness, travel, «لامستم») not glossed: the tafsirs word «لامستم» differently. STAGING v4: 6: a man sits, rises on 6:5 (rising to the prayer); no washing gesture, no body part, no water and no water symbol (6:8-17, camera only). He leaves on 6:15, so nobody is on screen for the major impurity, illness, need and touching (6:18-39, camera and wind only). On 6:40 a traveller (no water on a journey) walks in and sits; tayammum is not acted. He stands on 6:54 and prays after the light plate (6:56): standing, bowing, prostrating, then sitting on the gratitude word 6:61. 7: believers pray in a prayer hall (remembering the favour of what Allah legislated); nobody speaks on 7:10, as As-Sa'di says the pledge was not spoken but meant by their faith. Seal for the covenant, geometric on the Name 7:16, prostration before it, they sit on 7:18."
 },
